m(1,'A fraud model has excellent test results, but its features include the final investigation outcome, unavailable at prediction time. What should the engineer do?', 'Remove the outcome feature and rebuild a leakage-free split', [('Increase tree depth','Greater model capacity does not remove information leakage.'),('Use the test data for tuning','Tuning on the test set contaminates evaluation.'),('Scale every column','Scaling does not make a future outcome available at inference.')], 'Information learned after the prediction time leaks the target. Rebuild features using only information available then.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/how-it-works-mlconcepts.html','Could every input exist when the prediction is requested?')
m(1,'A support assistant must retrieve passages with similar meaning even when a query uses different wording. What should be indexed?', 'Text embeddings in a vector index with source metadata', [('Only the file names in a spreadsheet','File names do not represent passage meaning.'),('Only a hash of each document','Hashes detect identity, not semantic similarity.'),('An IAM role per sentence','Roles govern access rather than semantic retrieval.')], 'Embeddings encode semantic relationships; a vector index finds similar passages. Metadata supports filtering and provenance.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base.html','Think about representing meaning as numeric vectors.')
m(1,'A daily sales model will forecast future weeks. Which validation split best reflects deployment?', 'Train on earlier periods and validate on later periods', [('Randomly shuffle all rows across time','Future information may leak into a historical forecast experiment.'),('Validate on the exact training rows','Training performance is not generalization evidence.'),('Remove all timestamps and mix periods','Removing a column does not prevent time leakage in the split.')], 'Time-ordered splits test the realistic task of predicting observations that occur after the training period.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/how-it-works-mlconcepts.html','Which data would genuinely have been available in the past?')
m(2,'A company wants answers grounded in internal policies that change every day, with links to the source. Which approach is the best starting point?', 'Retrieval-augmented generation with a refreshed knowledge base', [('Fine-tune on yesterday’s policies as the only knowledge source','A tuned model is not a reliable daily source-of-truth store or citation mechanism.'),('Increase the model temperature','Randomness does not supply current policy evidence.'),('Remove retrieval to reduce context','Without retrieval, private current evidence is absent.')], 'RAG retrieves current policy passages at request time and supplies grounding context. Validate the answer and citations separately.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-base.html','Is the missing capability current knowledge or a new response style?')
m(2,'A classifier detects a rare, costly equipment failure. Missing a failure is much worse than inspecting a healthy machine. Which metric should receive particular attention?', 'Recall for the failure class', [('Overall accuracy alone','A majority-class model can appear accurate while missing failures.'),('Training duration alone','Training speed does not measure missed failures.'),('Token count','Token count does not measure classification false negatives.')], 'Recall measures the fraction of actual failures detected. Threshold selection should also consider false-positive inspection costs.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/clarify-model-monitor-model-quality.html','Which error represents a missed actual failure?')
m(3,'A retailer must score ten million records overnight. Results are needed tomorrow, and there is no interactive traffic. Which SageMaker option fits?', 'Batch Transform', [('A permanently provisioned real-time endpoint','An always-on endpoint is unnecessary for this offline job.'),('An agent action group','An action group exposes tools, not a large offline scoring job.'),('A training job without inference','Training fits model parameters; it does not perform the requested scoring workload.')], 'Batch Transform processes a known offline dataset without requiring a persistent inference endpoint.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/deploy-model-options.html','Do these records need an immediate response or a scheduled bulk job?')
m(3,'A prediction request has a large payload and can take several minutes. Clients can wait for an output in S3. Which option is a suitable fit?', 'SageMaker Asynchronous Inference', [('A synchronous low-latency endpoint as the default','The long-running queued workload better matches asynchronous inference.'),('S3 static website hosting','Object hosting cannot run model inference by itself.'),('A feature-store lookup alone','Reading features does not execute the prediction model.')], 'Asynchronous inference queues requests and delivers results asynchronously, including output stored in S3.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/async-inference.html','Can processing be queued rather than holding a connection open?')
m(3,'An ML pipeline should register a model only after its validation score exceeds a threshold. What is the appropriate workflow?', 'A SageMaker Pipeline condition step before model registration', [('Always register every model as approved','This skips the explicit quality gate.'),('Rename the artifact with the word approved','A name is not an evaluated condition or approval control.'),('Use a larger GPU for deployment','More compute does not implement a quality gate.')], 'A condition step evaluates a metric and branches to registration only when the acceptance criterion is met.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/build-and-manage-steps-types.html','Where should the pipeline branch on the evaluation result?')
m(4,'A live model sees a different distribution of input values than its training baseline. Which capability directly helps detect this?', 'SageMaker Model Monitor data quality monitoring', [('CloudTrail alone','API audit records do not compare feature distributions.'),('Only a larger endpoint instance','Capacity does not detect distribution change.'),('Disabling data capture','Without suitable observations it is harder to detect drift.')], 'Compare captured inference inputs with a validated baseline using monitoring checks. Investigate detected drift before assuming model retraining is the remedy.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor.html','Is the concern about API history, compute capacity, or the data itself?')
m(4,'An agent intermittently fails after invoking a shipping API. Which first step best isolates the failing orchestration stage?', 'Inspect agent traces and tool errors with correlated request identifiers', [('Fine-tune the model immediately','Training does not diagnose an external API failure.'),('Raise temperature','Randomness does not identify which tool call failed.'),('Delete all logs to reduce cost','Removing evidence makes investigation harder.')], 'Agent traces reveal orchestration and action-group interactions. Correlate tool latency, errors, and timeouts before choosing a fix; redact sensitive values.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/trace-events.html','Follow a request across its tool invocations.')
m(1,'A training job needs columnar analytics over selected columns in a large S3 data lake. Which format is a strong candidate?', 'Parquet', [('Uncompressed line-by-line prose','Free text lacks the desired columnar layout.'),('A screenshot of a spreadsheet','An image is not a columnar analytical data file.'),('An IAM policy document','An access policy is not a dataset storage format.')], 'Parquet stores columnar data and supports efficient projection and compression for analytical workloads.', 'athena/latest/ug/columnar-storage.html','Which option organizes data by column?')
m(1,'Training numeric features have very different scales. A distance-based algorithm is dominated by the largest-valued feature. What should be considered?', 'Fit a scaling transform on training data and apply it consistently', [('Fit a separate transform on each prediction request','Inconsistent transforms change the model’s input meaning.'),('Use the target label as another feature','This leaks the target into inputs.'),('Scale only the held-out test set','Training and inference would then use different representations.')], 'Distance-based methods can be sensitive to scale. Learn preprocessing parameters from training data and reuse them at validation and inference.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/data-wrangler-transform.html','How can all stages share a learned preprocessing rule?')
m(1,'An invoice dataset contains personal identifiers unnecessary for the prediction task. What is the best preparation step?', 'Remove or appropriately redact unnecessary personal data before training', [('Duplicate the identifiers in more columns','Duplicating sensitive data increases exposure.'),('Make the S3 bucket public for easier access','Public access is unrelated to necessary model features and exposes data.'),('Ignore privacy until deployment','Training datasets already create privacy exposure.')], 'Minimize sensitive data early. Preserve only necessary information and apply access controls and appropriate redaction.', 'comprehend/latest/dg/how-pii.html','Does the model need these identifiers to solve the task?')
m(1,'A RAG system retrieves chunks about unrelated product versions. The version is already stored as document metadata. What should the engineer try?', 'Filter retrieval using the requested product version', [('Remove all metadata','This removes the available disambiguation signal.'),('Increase generation randomness','Generation randomness does not filter retrieved documents.'),('Train the embedding model on passwords','Passwords are unrelated and sensitive.')], 'Metadata filters narrow the eligible evidence to the requested version before generation. Evaluate whether relevant passages remain retrievable.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-config.html','Which existing attribute distinguishes the relevant evidence?')
m(2,'A foundation model must consistently follow an organization’s output style. Current knowledge is already supplied through retrieval. What additional technique may help?', 'Supervised fine-tuning with representative input-output examples', [('Only increasing vector-index capacity','Index capacity does not directly teach a response style.'),('Removing all evaluation examples','Then style improvements cannot be measured reliably.'),('Disabling authorization checks','Access controls are unrelated to learning a style.')], 'Fine-tuning can adapt behavior using representative examples. Compare with a prompt-only baseline and evaluate quality and safety before adoption.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/model-customization.html','Is this a knowledge freshness issue or a response behavior issue?')
m(2,'A model scores extremely well on training data but poorly on unseen validation data. Which change could reduce overfitting?', 'Increase regularization and evaluate on untouched validation data', [('Increase model capacity without evaluation','A more complex model can worsen overfitting.'),('Report training accuracy as the production estimate','Training fit is not an unbiased generalization estimate.'),('Tune repeatedly on the final test set','This contaminates the final evaluation.')], 'Regularization constrains excessive fit to training examples. Select settings using validation, then reserve test data for final evaluation.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/automatic-model-tuning-how-it-works.html','How can model complexity be constrained?')
m(2,'Two summarization models need to be compared for factual accuracy on legal documents. Which evaluation is strongest?', 'A representative held-out set with human checks for unsupported claims', [('Token throughput alone','Speed does not establish factual accuracy.'),('One easy prompt used during tuning','A single familiar example gives weak generalization evidence.'),('The longest output always wins','Length is not correctness or faithfulness.')], 'Use representative cases and a documented rubric. Human evaluation can detect unsupported factual statements that surface-form metrics miss.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/evaluation.html','Which method actually checks the requested quality attribute?')
m(2,'A RAG assistant cannot answer because the relevant passage is absent from the top retrieved results. What should be evaluated first?', 'Retrieval quality, including chunking and relevant-document recall', [('Only the final model’s response length','The necessary evidence is missing before generation begins.'),('Only endpoint uptime','Availability does not establish evidence relevance.'),('Only training loss of an unrelated classifier','It does not measure this retrieval stage.')], 'Diagnose retrieval separately from generation. Relevant-document recall and inspection of chunks help locate evidence loss.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-test-retrieve.html','At which stage was the needed evidence lost?')
m(3,'A model release must be reproducible and auditable. Which record should be versioned together?', 'Code, preprocessing, data references, model artifact and configuration', [('Only the endpoint name','An endpoint name does not reproduce the training or deployment inputs.'),('Only the latest notebook output','This omits dependencies and artifact provenance.'),('Only the developer’s browser history','Browser history is not controlled model lineage.')], 'Reproducible releases depend on versioned inputs, transformations, artifacts and deployment settings, with lineage linking them.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/model-registry.html','What would another engineer need to reproduce this exact release?')
m(3,'A new endpoint model should receive a small portion of live traffic before broad rollout, with automatic rollback on alarms. What approach fits?', 'A canary deployment with monitored rollback criteria', [('Replace all traffic without observing metrics','That maximizes exposure before validation.'),('Change the training set during each request','This is not a controlled serving rollout.'),('Disable alarms during deployment','That defeats the requested automatic safety signal.')], 'Canary rollouts expose a limited fraction of traffic while operational and model-quality metrics determine promotion or rollback.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/deployment-guardrails.html','How can exposure be limited while learning from production traffic?')
m(3,'A Bedrock agent needs to call a business API to check order status. What should expose that capability?', 'An action group with the API schema and an authorized execution path', [('A longer system prompt with invented order statuses','Prompt text cannot query the live business system.'),('A second vector index containing random values','An index is not a live status tool.'),('A public administrator access key in the prompt','Exposing a privileged secret is unnecessary and unsafe.')], 'An action group describes callable operations; the execution path must enforce authorization, validate inputs and return actual business data.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/agents-action-create.html','What makes a tool callable rather than merely described in prose?')
m(3,'An inference endpoint receives predictable load spikes, with rising request latency and insufficient provisioned capacity. What should the engineer configure?', 'Appropriate automatic scaling with tested capacity limits and metrics', [('Randomly change the model’s class labels','Labels do not add serving capacity.'),('Disable all monitoring','Scaling needs operational signals.'),('Increase training epochs at request time','Training epochs are not serving capacity.')], 'Use workload-appropriate scaling signals and tested minimum/maximum capacity. Confirm latency, concurrency, and startup behavior under load.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/endpoint-auto-scaling.html','Is the bottleneck serving capacity or the prediction target?')
m(4,'An application role requires read access to one model-input prefix in S3. What should its policy grant?', 'Only the necessary object actions on that prefix, with needed key permissions', [('AdministratorAccess for convenience','Broad administrative rights exceed the required data access.'),('Anonymous public access to the entire bucket','This exposes data rather than authorizing only the workload.'),('All KMS keys and all buckets','Resource scope should match the actual requirement.')], 'Least privilege scopes actions and resources to the workload. Encrypted objects can also require permission to use the relevant KMS key.', 'AmazonS3/latest/userguide/security_iam_service-with-iam.html','What is the smallest access boundary that satisfies the task?')
m(4,'A team wants to investigate who changed a production model endpoint configuration. Which source is most directly relevant?', 'AWS CloudTrail API activity records', [('Only model prediction confidence','Confidence does not identify the caller of a configuration API.'),('Only the training confusion matrix','A confusion matrix evaluates predictions, not administrative activity.'),('Only a vector similarity score','Similarity is unrelated to configuration audit history.')], 'CloudTrail records supported AWS API activity, including identity and request context useful for configuration-change investigations.', 'awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-user-guide.html','Does the question ask about model quality or who made an API call?')
m(4,'A GenAI application’s token spend rises sharply. Which first action supports a sensible optimization decision?', 'Measure token usage and quality by request type, then test targeted changes', [('Always choose the smallest model regardless of quality','Lower unit cost can fail the business-quality requirement.'),('Remove all security controls','Security controls should not be traded away without justification.'),('Disable usage records','Then the cost increase cannot be attributed.')], 'Identify expensive request categories and test prompt/context length, model choice and caching where appropriate against a quality and latency baseline.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/monitoring.html','Which requests account for the cost, and what quality must be retained?')
m(4,'An input filter blocks many attacks, but some malicious prompts still reach an agent. Which design is most appropriate?', 'Use defense in depth, including tool authorization and output validation', [('Assume one guardrail eliminates all risks','No input filter guarantees complete protection.'),('Let the model authorize its own privileged tools','Authorization must be enforced by the execution system.'),('Place credentials in the system prompt','A prompt is not a secure credential store.')], 'Guardrails complement least privilege, input validation, protected secrets and enforcement at tool execution. Test adversarial and benign cases.', 'bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails.html','Which checks must still hold even when the model makes a mistake?')
m(1,'Repeated customer records appear in both training and test data. How should an engineer repair the evaluation?', 'Deduplicate and split at the customer or entity boundary as appropriate', [('Keep duplicates to inflate sample count','Repeated entities can leak information across the split.'),('Add the test label to the input','That directly leaks the answer.'),('Use only the training score','That does not repair held-out evaluation.')], 'Separate correlated entities where deployment requires generalization to new entities. Deduplication reduces accidental overlap.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/how-it-works-mlconcepts.html','Could the model recognize the same entity rather than generalize?')
m(2,'A training job searches candidate learning rates and tree depths automatically. What is this process?', 'Hyperparameter optimization using a validation objective', [('Inference logging','Logging records operation rather than searches model settings.'),('Encryption at rest','Encryption protects stored data rather than tunes model settings.'),('Vector retrieval','Retrieval finds similar items rather than chooses training settings.')], 'Hyperparameter optimization explores configurations to improve a chosen validation metric under resource constraints.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/automatic-model-tuning.html','Are these learned weights or settings supplied to the training process?')
m(3,'An ML workflow has preprocessing, training, evaluation, and conditional registration steps. Which service feature directly manages this sequence?', 'SageMaker Pipelines', [('Amazon Route 53 alone','DNS routing does not manage this ML step sequence.'),('AWS KMS alone','Key management does not orchestrate ML steps.'),('An S3 object tag alone','A tag is metadata, not an execution workflow.')], 'SageMaker Pipelines orchestrates dependent ML steps and records executions. Conditions can enforce evaluation gates.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/pipelines.html','Which option is an ML workflow orchestrator?')
m(4,'A classifier’s monitored input distribution is stable, but newly collected labels show lower precision. What should be investigated?', 'Model quality degradation using predictions joined with ground-truth labels', [('Assume stable inputs prove stable quality','Input stability does not guarantee an unchanged relationship to outcomes.'),('Delete the labels','Ground truth is needed to measure predictive quality.'),('Only increase log retention','Retention alone does not diagnose changed predictive performance.')], 'Model quality monitoring compares predictions with observed outcomes. Investigate data, target relationships and operating thresholds before deciding on retraining.', 'sagemaker/latest/dg/model-monitor-model-quality.html','Which evidence measures actual predictive correctness?')
