s(1,'An analyst’s large query spills to remote storage. Concurrency is low. What should be evaluated first?', 'A larger warehouse and the query’s execution plan', [('Only adding more clusters','Additional clusters primarily address concurrent workloads, not one query’s resource needs.'),('Disabling role checks','Permissions do not fix memory spill.'),('Changing a result column alias','Aliases do not supply compute capacity.')], 'Scaling up may give an individual query more resources. Inspect the profile and query design before committing to extra cost.', 'user-guide/warehouses-considerations','Is the pressure from one query or many simultaneous queries?')
s(1,'A warehouse suspends between jobs that run a few minutes apart. Which setting directly controls the idle delay?', 'AUTO_SUSPEND', [('INITIALLY_SUSPENDED','This controls the initial state when the warehouse is created.'),('AUTO_RESUME','This controls resumption when work arrives.'),('DATA_RETENTION_TIME_IN_DAYS','Retention controls historical data availability, not idle compute.')], 'AUTO_SUSPEND defines the idle interval before suspension. Balance repeated cold starts against idle cost.', 'sql-reference/sql/create-warehouse','Which setting specifies seconds of inactivity?')
s(1,'A warehouse should consume no compute immediately after it is created. Which property directly expresses this?', 'INITIALLY_SUSPENDED = TRUE', [('AUTO_RESUME = FALSE alone','This controls future automatic resumption, not the initial creation state.'),('A larger warehouse size','Size does not specify initial suspension.'),('A longer Time Travel window','Retention does not set warehouse startup state.')], 'INITIALLY_SUSPENDED controls whether the new warehouse is initially suspended.', 'sql-reference/sql/create-warehouse','Separate creation state from later idle behavior.')
s(1,'A team needs semantic retrieval over support documents in Snowflake. Which capability is designed for this search use case?', 'Cortex Search', [('Fail-safe','Fail-safe supports disaster recovery rather than semantic retrieval.'),('AUTO_SUSPEND','This manages warehouse idle behavior.'),('UNDROP','UNDROP restores dropped objects, not search relevance.')], 'Cortex Search provides low-latency hybrid retrieval over text, useful as a retrieval component for search and RAG.', 'user-guide/snowflake-cortex/cortex-search/cortex-search-overview','Which feature retrieves relevant text?')
s(2,'A role needs to query a table in an existing database and schema. Which combination is generally required?', 'USAGE on the database and schema, plus SELECT on the table', [('Only SELECT on the table with no parent access','Parent container USAGE is also needed for object access.'),('OWNERSHIP on every object in the account','Ownership is far broader than query access requires.'),('Only USAGE on the warehouse','Compute access alone does not grant data access.')], 'Data access follows container and object privileges. An executing role also needs access to an available warehouse when compute is required.', 'user-guide/security-access-control-overview','Think about parent containers as well as the data object.')
s(2,'A view should return only rows belonging to the current user’s business unit. Which policy is intended for this purpose?', 'Row access policy', [('Masking policy alone','Masking transforms visible column values rather than defines row visibility.'),('Resource monitor','Resource monitors govern credit consumption.'),('File format','File formats describe external data encoding.')], 'Row access policies determine whether a row is visible based on an expression and execution context.', 'user-guide/security-row-intro','Does the requirement hide rows or replace column values?')
s(2,'An auditor asks which identity authenticated and when. Where should an engineer start?', 'LOGIN_HISTORY or the corresponding account-usage login history', [('Only a table’s clustering depth','Clustering metadata does not record authentication events.'),('Only COPY_HISTORY','Load history tracks ingestion, not user login events.'),('Only the stage file list','A file list is not an authentication audit record.')], 'Login history provides authentication event information. Account Usage views can have latency, so choose the interface and time range appropriately.', 'sql-reference/functions/login_history','Identify the relevant event type before choosing a history view.')
s(2,'A team wants future tables in a schema to receive SELECT automatically for a reader role. What should it configure?', 'A future grant on tables in that schema', [('A single grant on one existing table only','An existing-object grant does not automatically cover future objects.'),('A larger warehouse','Compute sizing does not grant privileges.'),('A result cache','Caching does not define access control.')], 'Future grants define privileges to apply when new objects of the specified type are created. Existing objects need appropriate current grants too.', 'sql-reference/sql/grant-privilege','Does the grant concern today’s objects or objects not yet created?')
s(3,'A pipeline loads staged CSV files into a table using an explicit SQL command. Which command performs that load?', 'COPY INTO the target table', [('COPY INTO @stage as the target','A stage target represents unloading data out of a query or table.'),('GET on an external stage','GET downloads supported internal-stage files to a client.'),('UNDROP TABLE','UNDROP restores a dropped table.')], 'COPY INTO a table loads staged files. COPY INTO a location unloads query data.', 'sql-reference/sql/copy-into-table','Look at the command’s destination.')
s(3,'A CSV file has one header row that must not load as data. Which file-format option fits?', 'SKIP_HEADER = 1', [('STRIP_OUTER_ARRAY = TRUE','This is a JSON array handling option.'),('STRIP_NULL_VALUES = TRUE','This is associated with JSON handling, not skipping a CSV header.'),('AUTO_RESUME = TRUE','This is a warehouse property.')], 'SKIP_HEADER specifies the number of header lines to skip for CSV input.', 'sql-reference/sql/create-file-format','Which setting counts header lines?')
s(3,'A service needs files to be loaded automatically after they arrive in cloud storage. Which feature is intended for continuous file ingestion?', 'Snowpipe', [('Snowpipe Streaming as a file loader','Streaming ingests rows through its streaming interface rather than loads staged files in this pattern.'),('A row access policy','Access policies do not ingest files.'),('A secure view alone','A view does not watch cloud storage and load files.')], 'Snowpipe loads staged files continuously, commonly using cloud notifications for auto-ingest.', 'user-guide/data-load-snowpipe-intro','Are the arriving units files or rows sent through a streaming interface?')
s(3,'A load must record malformed rows for correction instead of silently accepting corrupted values. What is a useful first validation step?', 'Use COPY validation facilities and inspect errors before the production load', [('Ignore all errors and claim full completeness','Ignoring errors conceals missing or invalid records.'),('Disable all file-format definitions','Parsing still needs the correct format.'),('Use a larger warehouse as the only remedy','Compute sizing does not repair malformed records.')], 'Validation and error inspection help identify rejected records and parsing problems. Verify COPY option compatibility for the chosen load pattern.', 'sql-reference/sql/copy-into-table','How can parsing be checked before trusting the loaded row count?')
s(4,'A query needs a table’s state just before a known modifying statement. Which Time Travel clause fits?', 'BEFORE (STATEMENT => statement_id)', [('EXISTS (STATEMENT => statement_id)','EXISTS is not the Time Travel historical selector.'),('AUTO_SUSPEND','This controls idle compute, not historical table state.'),('ON (STATEMENT => statement_id)','ON is not the historical table reference syntax.')], 'BEFORE references the state immediately before the specified statement. AT supports other historical reference points.', 'user-guide/data-time-travel','Is the required state before or at a historical point?')
s(4,'A user drops a table by mistake while its retained history is still available. Which command can restore the dropped object?', 'UNDROP TABLE', [('DELETE TABLE','DELETE removes rows rather than restores a dropped table.'),('TRUNCATE TABLE','TRUNCATE removes table rows.'),('ALTER WAREHOUSE RESUME','Resuming compute does not restore data objects.')], 'UNDROP restores supported dropped objects during their Time Travel retention period, subject to naming and access constraints.', 'sql-reference/sql/undrop-table','Which command reverses a supported object drop?')
s(4,'A team clones a large table and makes no changes. Why does creating the clone avoid an immediate full data copy?', 'The clone initially references existing micro-partitions', [('The clone contains no rows','A table clone includes a consistent snapshot of the source data.'),('The warehouse compresses and exports every row first','A full export is not the zero-copy clone mechanism.'),('All retention protection is disabled','Retention is not what makes initial cloning zero-copy.')], 'Zero-copy cloning initially shares underlying storage. Later changes can create additional storage consumption.', 'user-guide/object-clone','Separate logical independence from initial physical storage sharing.')
s(4,'A warehouse was just resumed and a filter reads only a tiny fraction of the table’s micro-partitions. Which explanation best fits?', 'Metadata-based micro-partition pruning', [('The resumed warehouse must have a warm local cache','Suspension drops the warehouse cache.'),('Automatic clustering rewrites rows during every query','Clustering maintenance is not a per-query row rewrite step.'),('Every partition was fully read anyway','The profile states that only a small fraction was scanned.')], 'Snowflake uses partition metadata to exclude partitions that cannot satisfy the predicate. Pruning can work with a cold warehouse cache.', 'user-guide/tables-clustering-micropartitions','Which mechanism avoids reading irrelevant partitions?')
s(5,'A consumer queries shared data from a provider’s account. Who typically supplies compute for those queries?', 'The consumer’s warehouse', [('The provider always pays consumer query compute','Consumers normally use their own compute; reader-account arrangements differ.'),('No compute is required for any shared query','Sharing avoids copying data, not all computation.'),('Only the original loading warehouse','The original load warehouse is not tied to future consumer queries.')], 'Secure Data Sharing lets consumers query provider data using their own compute without copying the shared data into their account.', 'user-guide/data-sharing-intro','Separate storage ownership from query compute.')
s(5,'A team must run SQL on a schedule. Which Snowflake object is designed to schedule that execution?', 'Task', [('Stream alone','A stream tracks change data but does not by itself schedule SQL execution.'),('Stage','A stage identifies file storage.'),('File format','A file format describes parsing or serialization.')], 'Tasks run SQL on a schedule or under supported triggers and can form task graphs.', 'user-guide/tasks-intro','Which object runs work rather than stores files or tracks changes?')
s(5,'An incremental transformation needs to track row-level changes since its last consumption. Which object is most relevant?', 'Stream', [('Warehouse','A warehouse supplies compute rather than a change-tracking offset.'),('Masking policy','Masking transforms values for access control.'),('Stage','Stages hold or reference files rather than track table change offsets.')], 'A stream exposes supported change-data-capture information between transactional points for downstream processing.', 'user-guide/streams-intro','Is the requirement scheduling work or identifying changed rows?')
